---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "@/components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "@/components/Footer.astro";
import { SITE } from "@/config";

export const prerender = false;
---

<Layout
  title={`Privacy | ${SITE.title}`}
  description="How berryhill.dev handles analytics, local browser preferences, and contact links."
>
  <Header />
  <main id="main-content" class="privacy-page">
    <p class="prompt">guest@berryhill:~ $ cat privacy.md</p>
    <h1>Privacy at berryhill.dev</h1>
    <p>
      This page describes the public site's current source-backed behavior. It
      is not a claim about the data practices of sites you visit through
      external links.
    </p>
    <h2>Analytics and browser storage</h2>
    <p>
      In production, when PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID is configured, the site loads
      Google Analytics 4 via Google Tag Manager's gtag.js and sends page-view
      events. Google may set cookies or process usage information under its own
      policies. We do not claim this site has zero trackers. If the measurement
      ID is absent, this integration is not loaded.
    </p>
    <p>
      The site's theme control, where available, stores your theme preference in
      localStorage. Navigation may store a back-link in sessionStorage. These
      browser values are used for interface behavior, not submitted through a
      site contact form.
    </p>
    <h2>Contact and other services</h2>
    <p>
      The site links to email, Calendly, LinkedIn, and RSS. If you email us,
      your message goes through your mail provider; if you follow a third-party
      link, that provider's own privacy practices apply. There is no public
      contact submission form on this site. Server and hosting logs, retention,
      analytics configuration, and any third-party service settings require
      operator review before more specific promises can be made.
    </p>
    <p>
      For privacy questions, <a href="mailto:matt@berryhill.dev"
        >email Matt at matt@berryhill.dev</a
      >. See <a href="/about/">About</a> or <a href="/">return home</a>.
    </p>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .privacy-page {
    max-width: 48rem;
    margin: 3rem auto;
    padding: 0 1.5rem 4rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .privacy-page h1,
  .privacy-page h2 {
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }
  .privacy-page .prompt {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-family: monospace;
  }
  .privacy-page a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
</style>
